  "id": "V028",
  "description": "A perfect 3-cycle gives every finalist the same Copeland score, so rung 2 decides: the higher-approved finalist wins",
  "spec_clause": "Phase 2 / Tally: 'Cycles are possible (A beats B beats C beats A) and must be handled rather than left to crash. Resolve in order: 1 Copeland score, 2 Approval count, 3 Rotation fairness, 4 Shortest runtime, 5 Seeded random.'",
  "rationale": "3 attendees, all three movies have all 3 rows (coverage 1.00, attendee_votes 3 >= 3). m1: 3 yes -> approval 3/3 = 1.00. m2: 2 yes -> 2/3 = 0.6667. m3: 2 yes -> 0.6667. All clear the floor; ranked m1 (3 yes), then m2 and m3 tie on 2 yes with equal approval, fairness tied (u2 and u3 both never won, same join date), so runtime orders them: m2 105 < m3 110. Round robin: m1 vs m2 = 2 (u1,u2) to 1 (u3) -> m1; m2 vs m3 = 2 (u1,u2) to 1 (u3) -> m2; m1 vs m3 = 1 (u2) to 2 (u1,u3) -> m3. That is the cycle m1 > m2 > m3 > m1, so no Condorcet winner. Rung 1 Copeland: m1 = 1, m2 = 1, m3 = 1 -> three-way tie, cannot decide. Rung 2 approval: m1 1.00 > m2 0.6667 = m3 0.6667 -> unique maximum -> winner m1.",
